1
00:05:23,478 --> 00:05:29,478
Experience it. Enjoy it. Just don't fall for it.

2
00:10:46,956 --> 00:10:52,956
Almost Famous is a drama, music film directed by Cameron Crowe.

3
00:16:10,434 --> 00:16:16,434
In 1973, 15-year-old William Miller's unabashed love of music and aspiration to become a rock journalist lands him an
assignment from Rolling Stone magazine to interview and tour with the up-and-coming band, Stillwater.

4
00:21:33,913 --> 00:21:39,913
Russell Hammond, played by Billy Crudup.

5
00:26:57,391 --> 00:27:03,391
Elaine Miller, played by Frances McDormand.

6
00:32:20,869 --> 00:32:26,869
Penny Lane, played by Kate Hudson.

7
00:37:44,347 --> 00:37:50,347
Jeff Bebe, played by Jason Lee.

8
00:43:07,826 --> 00:43:13,826
William Miller, played by Patrick Fugit.

9
00:48:31,304 --> 00:48:37,304
Anita Miller, played by Zooey Deschanel.

10
00:53:54,782 --> 00:54:00,782
Almost Famous is a 2000 American comedy drama film written and directed by Cameron Crowe, starring
Billy Crudup, Frances McDormand, Kate Hudson, Patrick Fugit, and Philip Seymour Hoffman.

11
00:59:18,260 --> 00:59:24,260
It tells the story of a teenage journalist, played by Fugit, writing for Rolling Stone magazine in the early 1970s,
touring with the fictitious rock band Stillwater, and writing his first cover story on the band.

12
01:04:41,739 --> 01:04:47,739
The film is semi-autobiographical, based on Crowe's
experiences as a teenage writer for Rolling Stone.

13
01:10:05,217 --> 01:10:11,217
The film performed poorly in theaters, grossing $47.4
million against a $60 million budget.

14
01:15:28,695 --> 01:15:34,695
It was widely acclaimed by critics and earned four Academy Award
nominations, including a win for Best Original Screenplay.

15
01:20:52,173 --> 01:20:58,173
It also won the 2001 Grammy Award for Best Compilation Soundtrack Album
for a Motion Picture, Television or Other Visual Media.

16
01:26:15,652 --> 01:26:21,652
Roger Ebert hailed it as the best film of the year
and the ninth-best film of the 2000s.

17
01:31:39,130 --> 01:31:45,130
The film also won two Golden Globe Awards, one for Best Motion Picture – Musical or
Comedy and another for Best Supporting Actress – Motion Picture for Hudson.

18
01:37:02,608 --> 01:37:08,608
The film is regarded by some as a cult classic and in a 2016 international poll conducted by the  BBC, Almost Famous was ranked the
79th-greatest film since 2000, while it was ranked as the 47th-best film of the 21st century in a 2025 poll by The New York Times.

19
01:42:26,086 --> 01:42:32,086
In a Hollywood Reporter 2014 list voted on by "studio chiefs, Oscar winners and TV
royalty", Almost Famous was ranked the 71st-greatest film of all time.

20
01:47:49,565 --> 01:47:55,565
A stage musical adaptation of the film opened on Broadway in November 2022.

21
01:53:13,043 --> 01:53:19,043
The film explores themes of hotel room, concert, rock
'n' roll, stewardess, drug addiction.

22
01:58:36,521 --> 01:58:42,521
The tone is emotional.
